# DNA100C vendor HID - CONNECT AND DOWNLOAD TRANSCRIPT
# Captured 2026-10-30, RE-IDENTIFIED 2026-10-31.
#
# WAS NAMED hid-idle-baseline.log AND DESCRIBED AS IDLE TELEMETRY. THAT WAS
# WRONG. This is EScribe's "Connect and Download Settings" sequence.
#
# What corrected it: a 123-second capture on 2026-10-31 with EScribe open
# and connected the whole time produced device traffic in ONE 7-second
# window - the reconnect - and silence for the other 116 seconds. The
# DNA100C sends nothing on USB unless EScribe asks. There is no idle poll
# loop, so there was no idle to baseline.
#
# The 207 request/reply pairs here are one complete connect-and-download:
#   requests  207 frames /  2,549 payload bytes
#   replies   207 frames / 10,011 payload bytes
# Every connect observed produces the same 207 pairs; separate captures
# differ only in a handful of counter bytes.
#
# This also resolves the caveat added to kb/16 on 2026-10-30, which doubted
# the settings-transfer section because 30s of "idle" held exactly 207
# F8 2B frames - the same count as a transfer. Same count because it was
# the same operation. The section was right; the caveat was the error.
#
# Frame: 01 DE <inner_len> <op hi> <op lo> <inner_len payload bytes>
#   f82a = host -> device (request)
#   f82b = device -> host (reply)
#
# For the WRITE direction see hid-write-group.log in this directory.
#
# USB descriptors and control frames are EXCLUDED: the string descriptors
# in a raw capture carry the device serial (kb/12). Raw .pcapng files stay
# out of this repo for that reason.
#
# First 40 exchanges of 207 total.

